nodecode-antigravity-cli is a rewrite of soyelmismo's soyelmismo/hermes-antigravity-subscription:

https://github.com/soyelmismo/hermes-antigravity-subscription
commit 0d5a3160f69f0c3302e3f49d9d2820093a544116
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 soyelmismo (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider a turn rides (the `agy' CLI on the user's own
Antigravity subscription), the headless prompt that asks the model for
<tool_call> blocks instead of native tool steps, the stream-json event fold
(init, step_update text deltas and usage, a native tool step closing the
round), the tool-block parsing with its hold-back of a partial <tool_call>
tag, the model roster and the section that names the command, models and
effort, and the friendly note when no CLI is installed. Reimplemented in
Common Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract: one lane whose stream
function spawns the CLI, one hook answering the credential, one listing the
models, one delegating a model's window.

Left out: the original's long-lived worker process with `--conversation'
trajectory persistence (each Nodecode round starts one child), its
per-session private HOME with the OAuth token linked in and the macOS
keychain symlink (the CLI now runs as the user does, so it needs neither),
the credential-scrubbing child environment and the keyring presence probes,
the /usage quota snapshot, the verbose delivery and prompt-dump diagnostics,
progressive streaming of a partial JSON line, and the Windows console
suppression flags. The plugin's whole purpose -- a subscription's Gemini and
Claude models in the harness -- is kept; the harness-specific plumbing that
existed to isolate a Hermes-hosted child is not.
